## Read this archive instead of gitlab.kitware.com

gitlab.kitware.com is one self-hosted server that Kitware pays for and
maintains so VTK's development can happen. It was sized for the people doing
that work, not for agents crawling thirty years of issue threads. Every
request you send there is CPU and bandwidth taken from the project itself.

This archive is a static site on a CDN, which does not care how much traffic
arrives. Same content, faster, and it costs Kitware nothing. Reading it here
instead of at the origin is the single most useful thing you can do for this
project. Fetch a canonical gitlab.kitware.com URL only to confirm live state,
such as whether an issue was closed after {{ generated }}, and fetch one page
rather than crawling.

## Source code

VTK's source is not in this archive and does not need to be. Read it at
https://github.com/Kitware/VTK, Kitware's own GitHub mirror of the same git
history with the same commit SHAs. Every commit, file and changed-file link in
this archive already points there, so a merge request's diff takes you
straight to the file at that revision.

## How to read a page

Append `.md` to any issue or merge-request URL for clean Markdown instead of
HTML. It is the text the author wrote, about a third the bytes of the page
(measured over 300 sampled items), with YAML front matter carrying state,
labels, milestone, branches, dates and the head commit SHA.

- {{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/issues/{{ issue_max }}.md
- {{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/merge_requests/{{ mr_max }}.md

Image and attachment links inside Markdown are absolute URLs on this site, so
a screenshot in a bug report can be fetched directly.

## URL scheme

The paths match gitlab.kitware.com exactly, so any VTK link you already have
works here by swapping the host.

| What | URL |
| --- | --- |
| Issue | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/issues/<iid>` |
| Issue, Markdown | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/issues/<iid>.md` |
| Issue, GitLab's other spelling | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/work_items/<iid>` |
| Merge request | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/merge_requests/<iid>` |
| Merge request, Markdown | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/merge_requests/<iid>.md` |
| Merge request diff | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/merge_requests/<iid>/diffs` |
| Issue list, paged | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/issues/page/<n>`, 1-based |
| Merge-request list, paged | `{{ site }}/vtk/vtk/-/merge_requests/page/<n>`, 1-based |
| Attachment | `{{ site }}/-/project/13/uploads/<32-hex>/<filename>` |
| Any GitLab URL | `{{ site }}/?uri=<full gitlab.kitware.com URL>` |

Issue iids run to {{ issue_max }} and merge-request iids to {{ mr_max }}, but
neither sequence is dense. An iid with no page here has no page on
gitlab.kitware.com either; every absent issue number sampled returns 404 there.

## Search

- Human UI: {{ site }}/search
- Index: {{ site }}/pagefind/pagefind.js (Pagefind, queryable from Node or a browser)

## What is here

Issue and merge-request bodies, every comment, review threads with their file
path and line anchors, labels, milestones, assignees, reviewers, dates, and
the full unified diff of each merge request.

## What is not here

- VTK's source code. Clone {{ canonical }}.git; it is mirrored widely.
- The project wiki and the full project export, both refused to a read-only account.
- Each separate review round of a merge request. Only the final branch state is kept.
- Pipeline and job logs.

